research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/proposed-inventory.json:4951:      "candidate_contract": "Candidate items: `def-aqft-anomaly-matching-data`; `prop-aqft-heavy-chiral-threshold-wess-zumino-match`; and `ex-aqft-heavy-fermion-anomaly-threshold`, but only after the gauge/anomaly researcher supplies the exact local definitions, anomaly normalization, and hypotheses. Reuse `qftx-bv-brst`, `qftx-anomaly-cocycles`, and `def-qftx-chiral-anomaly-interface` at their actual Abelian/scalar or purely mathematical interfaces. `D'Hoker–Farhi` and Wess–Zumino/Witten sources are candidate literature inputs; any coefficient-level statement must identify representations, symmetry breaking, regulator, descent convention, and admissible local counterterms. The current local QFT item does not prove the general non-Abelian threshold-matching statement.",
