research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/scaffold/proposed-inventory.json:5055:      "candidate_contract": "| `exp-aqft-atlas-global-smeft-fit-2026` | ATLAS Collaboration, arXiv:2604.21670v2 (10 Jun 2026), published JHEP 2026. Inputs include Run 2 Higgs/STXS and di-Higgs measurements, WW/WZ/VBF-Zjj, high-mass Drell–Yan, top distributions, and LEP/SLD/ATLAS electroweak precision observables. The report simultaneously constrains 48 Warsaw coefficients/linear combinations and states no significant deviations from the SM. It gives full likelihood and simplified likelihood outputs. | Preserve source's 13 TeV and input-specific 36–140 fb⁻¹ luminosities, event-overlap study, detector/theory/statistical uncertainties and correlations. It notes an electroweak-precision direction is pulled by the established `A_FB^b`/`A_FB^c` versus SM discrepancy; do not paraphrase the abstract as every coefficient lying within `2 sigma`. No event-level data or full subanalysis calibration audit has been reconstructed here; the full individual source analyses remain relevant for apparatus detail. |",
