This page is an interface, not a substitute for the gauge specialist's anomaly work. Define local gauge anomaly, anomaly polynomial/descent data, background/global symmetry anomaly, admissible counterterm, and Wess–Zumino functional in the exact chosen model. Distinguish an inconsistent gauge redundancy (which blocks the proposed quantum gauge theory absent a specified cancellation mechanism) from a global 't Hooft anomaly that an infrared effective theory must reproduce. When integrating out heavy chiral matter, state how its mass is generated and what degrees of freedom, Goldstone fields, or topological terms remain; ordinary power-suppressed decoupling is not automatic for anomaly data.

