## Statement

Use the heavy chiral "'$U(1)_X$ model with $M_H=|y|v>0$, background curvature $F=dA$, transformations $A'"\\mapsto A+d\\alpha"'$ and $'"\\theta\\mapsto\\theta+\\alpha"'$, and the fixed consistent-anomaly counterterm convention defined on this page. Adopt the source-derived Pauli–Villars consistent-anomaly formula for a positive-chirality Weyl field: $'"\\delta_\\alpha\\Gamma_R=-\\frac{1}{24\\pi"'^2}'"\\int_M\\operatorname{tr}_R\\"'!'"\\left(\\alpha\\,d\\left(A\\wedge dA-\\frac{i}{2}A\\wedge A\\wedge A\\right)\\right)"'$, in Bilal'"'s Hermitian gauge convention. For the one-dimensional charge-one representation and Abelian background, the cubic term vanishes and "'$'"\\operatorname{tr}_R(1)=1"'$, so the heavy-sector variation is $'"\\mathcal A_H(\\alpha,A)=-\\frac{1}{24\\pi"'^2}'"\\int_M\\alpha F\\wedge F"'$. If $'"\\Gamma_L"'$ is any specified remaining-light-sector functional with variation $'"\\mathcal A_L"'$, and the low-energy theory retains $'"\\theta"'$ at external momenta $E'"\\ll M_H"'$ and is required to match this perturbative background anomaly, then the local term

$$'"\\Gamma_{\\mathrm{WZ}}[A,\\theta]=-\\frac{1}{24\\pi"'^2}'"\\int_M\\theta F\\wedge F"'$$

satisfies $'"\\delta_\\alpha\\Gamma_{\\mathrm{WZ}}=\\mathcal A_H"'$ and therefore $'"\\delta_\\alpha(\\Gamma_L+\\Gamma_{\\mathrm{WZ}})=\\mathcal A_L+\\mathcal A_H=\\delta_\\alpha(\\Gamma_L+\\Gamma_H)"'$. The coefficient has no $M_H''^{-1}$ factor. This is a local perturbative anomaly-matching statement in the chosen representative; it does not assert a global determinant phase, cancellation of a dynamical gauge anomaly, a gravitational contribution, convergence of the EFT expansion, or a continuum interacting QFT.

## Statement references

