      "proposed_proof": "**Given:** The model and transformation conventions, the algebraic representation-trace convention, the source-derived consistent-anomaly input, and the low-energy anomaly-matching requirement.\n\n[F1] [[def-aqft-heavy-chiral-u1-threshold-data]]: the background is Abelian with $F=dA$, the Goldstone phase shifts by $\\delta_\\alpha\\theta=\\alpha$, and the chosen heavy pair has charges $1$ and $0$ with $M_H=|y|v>0$.\n\n[F2] [[def-qftx-chiral-anomaly-interface]]: for a one-dimensional charge-one representation, the trace of the cubic generator is $1$; the supplier's $d^{111}$ is twice the symmetrized trace and is only algebraic representation data, not itself a physical anomaly formula.\n\n[A1] Adopt the source-derived consistent anomaly representative for a positive-chirality Weyl determinant in the specified Pauli–Villars scheme, with no non-gauge-invariant local counterterm added. The exact formula and conventions are stated in the Statement and sourced to Bilal, §5.2.3, Eq. (5.45), and §9.3, Eq. (9.30).\n\n[A2] At external momenta $E\\ll M_H$, the EFT retains the shifting field $\\theta$ and must reproduce the same local background-$U(1)_X$ anomaly as the ultraviolet heavy determinant. This matching requirement does not assert that the model has a nonperturbative continuum construction.\n\n\n\n**Given:** [F1], [F2], [A1], and [A2].\n\n1.1 From [F1], $F'=d(A+d\\alpha)=F+d^2\\alpha=F$, and $\\delta_\\alpha\\theta=\\alpha$. Thus $F\\wedge F$ is invariant under the specified small background transformations. [given, F1, algebra]\n\n2.1 Apply [A1] in the charge-one representation of [F2]. Since $A$ is an Abelian scalar one-form, $A\\wedge A=0$ and $A\\wedge A\\wedge A=0$; hence $d(A\\wedge dA)=dA\\wedge dA=F\\wedge F$. The neutral opposite-chirality partner contributes zero cubic charge. Therefore $\\delta_\\alpha\\Gamma_H=-\\frac{1}{24\\pi^2}\\int_M\\alpha F\\wedge F=\\mathcal A_H(\\alpha,A)$. [given, F2, A1, step 1.1, algebra]\n\n3.1 Vary the displayed local functional: $\\delta_\\alpha\\Gamma_{\\mathrm{WZ}}=-\\frac{1}{24\\pi^2}\\int_M\\left((\\delta_\\alpha\\theta)F\\wedge F+\\theta\\,\\delta_\\alpha(F\\wedge F)\\right)=-\\frac{1}{24\\pi^2}\\int_M\\alpha F\\wedge F=\\mathcal A_H(\\alpha,A)$ by step 1.1 and step 2.1. [F1, A1, step 1.1, step 2.1, algebra]\n\n4.1 For the same light functional $\\Gamma_L$, linearity of the infinitesimal variation gives $\\delta_\\alpha(\\Gamma_L+\\Gamma_{\\mathrm{WZ}})=\\mathcal A_L+\\mathcal A_H=\\delta_\\alpha(\\Gamma_L+\\Gamma_H)$ by step 3.1 and the definition of $\\mathcal A_L$. This is the required local anomaly match under [A2]. [A2, step 2.1, step 3.1, algebra]\n\n5.1 The coefficient in $\\Gamma_{\\mathrm{WZ}}$ is the fixed dimensionless number $-1/(24\\pi^2)$ from [A1] and contains no factor of $M_H^{-1}$; only the validity condition $E\\ll M_H$ depends on the threshold. Thus the anomaly-carrying term is not power-suppressed in the heavy-mass expansion, without any claim of convergence or a quantitative remainder bound. [A1, A2, step 3.1, algebra] ∎\n\n\n\nThe current batch-41 manifest has no item carriers for the planned definitions of the background anomaly and anomaly-matching data. Their exact planned contracts are the background-gauge variation modulo a specified local-counterterm class, with dynamical-gauge inconsistency separated from explicit breaking, and the A6 interface fixing the model, representation, regulator, descent convention, and local matching criterion. They are formulation prerequisites only in this proof; their statements and proof status have not been treated as established. The separate batch-42 global-anomaly page is also absent, and this theorem makes no global claim. Readiness therefore remains escalated until the actual upstream carriers exist and their interfaces are checked.\n\n\n\n[[def-aqft-thooft-anomaly|Planned background-anomaly definition; no current carrier or readiness record]]\n\n[[def-aqft-anomaly-matching-data|Planned matching-data definition; no current carrier or readiness record]]"
