15:## Completed item: `def-aqft-global-anomaly-holonomy`
17:**Claim and conventions.** Defines the inverse determinant-line holonomy for a smooth Fredholm family of chiral Dirac operators on compact closed even-dimensional Riemannian spin manifolds, with a fixed unitary representation, Quillen metric, Bismut–Freed connection, endpoint gauge identification, and fixed regularization/counterterm convention. The phase is in (U(1)). Its planned direct supplier is `def-aqft-thooft-anomaly`, currently absent as above, so this item remains conditional.
21:**Sources read.** Dai–Freed, *Eta-Invariants and Determinant Lines*, §§1–2 and §5, PDF pp. 1–3, 8–15, 31–35, especially the inverse determinant line and the proof identifying adiabatic eta parallel transport with the Bismut–Freed connection: <https://arxiv.org/pdf/hep-th/9405012>. Freed, *Lectures on Field Theory and Topology*, Lecture 11 §§11.1–11.2, PDF pp. 154–163, for Pfaffian/determinant lines and anomaly-line context: <https://abel.math.harvard.edu/~dafr/CBMS133.pdf>. The lecture notes explicitly distinguish their rigorous sections from the thesis discussion in §11.4; no claim from §11.4 is used as a proved theorem. Full-body fetch stamps and source dispositions are still to be recorded.
23:**Proof status and next action.** The local proof checks finite-dimensional determinant-line fibers and that unitary parallel transport plus the endpoint gauge arrow gives a frame-independent unit phase. Next: author `def-aqft-anomaly-inflow-relative-theory`, then the conditional SU(2) phase/inflow theorem and worked B example; record exact supplier excerpts, source retrieval stamps, proof contracts, and readiness dispositions after all four carriers are present.
25:## Completed item: `def-aqft-anomaly-inflow-relative-theory`
27:**Claim and conventions.** Defines a spin boundary/bulk pair using the outward-normal-first boundary orientation. The bulk boundary line is the dual of the boundary anomaly line, and cancellation on a specified background loop is the equation `Hol_boundary * Hol_bulk = 1`. A `tikzcd` square illustrates the evaluation/parallel-transport condition; the proof states the line-duality argument without relying on the diagram. No bulk existence is asserted.
29:**Dependencies.** `def-aqft-global-anomaly-holonomy` (same-batch definition, level 1) and `def-aqft-thooft-anomaly` (planned batch-41 formulation prerequisite, exact item currently absent). Its planned level is 2. The missing batch-41 definition remains an explicit unresolved input.
31:**Sources read.** Freed, *Lectures on Field Theory and Topology*, Lecture 11 §§11.1–11.2, PDF pp. 154–163, for Pfaffian lines and the relative/invertible-theory interface; Dai–Freed, §5, PDF pp. 31–35, for determinant-line parallel transport and holonomy. §11.4 of Freed is identified as a thesis section and is not used as a proved result. Fetch/check stamps remain pending.
33:**Proof status and next action.** The two proof steps establish scalar evaluation from dual lines and the holonomy cancellation criterion. This item remains conditional on the missing `def-aqft-thooft-anomaly` carrier. The A theorem and B example are now authored; the next action is to synchronize the manifest/contracts/coverage, record source fetch stamps and escalated readiness, and run the scoped checks.
35:## Completed item: `pthm-aqft-global-anomaly-test`
