## Current supplier state and decisions

The latest `loadStep1Record`/`step1Decision` audit was run after the batch-41 inventory changed. The `qftx-thooft-anomalies` page and actual item carriers are present and registered in `research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23-batch-41.pages.json`; the global-anomaly page and its four item carriers are present and registered in batch 42. For `def-aqft-thooft-anomaly`, `def-aqft-anomaly-matching-data`, `def-aqft-cubic-anomaly-polynomial`, `def-aqft-global-anomaly-holonomy`, and `def-aqft-anomaly-inflow-relative-theory`, `step1Decision` currently returns **Readiness record missing**. This is an active readiness-record gap; the carriers' draft labels or pending independent approvals are not treated as mathematical defects.

The actual `def-aqft-thooft-anomaly` defines the local background class in `H^{1,4}(s|d_H)` modulo the model's admitted four-dimensional counterterms and distinguishes a background global symmetry from a dynamical gauge redundancy. The actual `def-aqft-anomaly-matching-data` specifies the matching group, representation and regulator/descent input as an adopted source-backed one-loop law, not a locally derived continuum theorem. Its displayed rules `B→B+dα`, `sB=dη`, and `sψ+=−iηψ+` for charge one determine the same real-parameter ghost replacement as the local model's `ψ+→e^{-iα}ψ+`; in Bilal's notation this is `ε=−α` and the anti-Hermitian variables are `iB`, `iα`. The coefficient is nevertheless fixed directly from Bilal's consistent formula rather than inferred from the match-data descent. Readiness remains escalated because current records for both direct batch-41 definitions and the transitive cubic-polynomial supplier are missing; there is no unresolved convention mismatch.

Transitive batch-41 inspection: the matching-data item depends on `def-aqft-cubic-anomaly-polynomial`, whose carrier is also now registered but whose current Step 1 record is missing. Its BRST prerequisites `def-aqft-p-form-global-symmetry`, `def-qftx-local-brst-cohomology`, `def-qftx-nonabelian-brst-complex`, and `lem-qftx-nonabelian-brst-nilpotence` were inspected; the relevant local/p-form/BRST interfaces and proofs were read. These transitive observations are recorded here, not as direct batch-44 dependency rows. The current global-anomaly statement is a conditional SU(2) mod-two test and is not used to infer any global result in batch 44.

The local definition, theorem, and dependent example therefore receive `escalated` Step 1 records after scoped authoring. The definition's direct matching-data input is not currently readiness-closed; the theorem has both direct batch-41 item inputs open, with the convention conversion checked; the example inherits the theorem's unresolved readiness prerequisite. No `--owner` record is used. A later source recheck clarified that the ghost conversion is determined by the actual equations, so the three local records below preserve the same `escalated` decisions while refreshing their current evidence and hashes.

## Source harvest and fetch evidence

Two independent full-text lecture-note treatments were read for the A page, with complete relevant arguments:

- Adel Bilal, [*Lectures on Anomalies*](https://arxiv.org/pdf/0802.0634), full 108-page PDF. Read §8.2, Eqs. (8.20)–(8.25), for Hermitian/anti-Hermitian connection, parameter, and fermion conventions; §5.2.3, Eqs. (5.32)–(5.46), including the opposite-statistics PV fields, mass cancellation condition `M₂²=M₁²+M₃²`, regulated triangle, positive-chirality cubic trace, and anomaly coefficient; and §9.3, Eqs. (9.16)–(9.30), for the complete consistent-anomaly completion. These passages directly support the formula and its conversion used here.
- John Preskill, [*Gauge Anomalies in an Effective Field Theory*](https://preskill.caltech.edu/pubs/preskill-1991-effective.pdf), full 78-page PDF. Read the complete §6.3–6.4 route, Eqs. (6.34)–(6.45): the Goldstone-dependent Yukawa mass, chiral change of variables, anomalous Jacobian, mass-independent gauge variation after integrating out the heavy fermion, and local Wess–Zumino interpretation. Its broader gauged `G/H`, cutoff, and gauge-consistency conclusions are not imported into this nondynamical `U(1)_V` model.

The search also found D’Hoker–Farhi's 1984 electroweak decoupling paper. Only its abstract/opening scope was inspected; it was not harvested because its `SU(2)_L` electroweak/global-soliton model is not this selected Abelian background computation. No full reading is claimed. No source retrieval failed, so no `source_resolution` drop/escalation record was required. `batch-44.coverage.json` records each source URL, exact locator, per-item disposition and limitation, search, retrieval attempt, and fetch stamp. The `source-fetch-check --stamp` result is recorded after the final source metadata synchronization.

